{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgAqoXM8HFWekeu8GoErY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016gMT3rMMbre1m5u1HMYsto","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/h-Kf8Lbf/ANSWER.md","content":"# Ticket #4471: why new-UI users have no session replays\n\n## Cause\n\nReplay is built from screenshots taken by `PostHogWidget`. The legacy shell\n(`lib/legacy_app.dart`) wraps its `MaterialApp` in `PostHogWidget`. The new\nshell (`lib/new_app.dart`) builds `MaterialApp.router` without it. So the new\nUI sends events (screens, taps, `loan_amount_changed`, `application_submitted`)\nbut no frames, and the Replay tab only has sessions from the old UI.\n\nEvidence:\n- `posthog_flutter` 5.55.0 source (`lib/src/posthog_widget.dart`): the widget's\n  state creates the `ScreenshotCapturer` and `NativeCommunicator` that feed\n  replay. Nothing else in the package produces replay frames on mobile.\n- Ticket: project settings are fine (recording on, sampling 100%, minimum\n  duration 0) and both groups use the same SDK version and build. The only\n  code difference between the groups is the wrapper.\n- `main.dart` calls `Analytics.init()` (which calls `Posthog().setup`) before\n  `runApp`, so the widget finds a config and starts capturing. Setup order is\n  not the cause.\n\n## Fix\n\n`lib/new_app.dart`: wrapped `MaterialApp.router` in `PostHogWidget` and added a\ncomment saying why it must stay. `dart format` also reflowed the `theme:`\nblock onto one line.\n\nNo other files changed.\n\n## Which parts of the colleague's note applied\n\nApplied:\n- The core diagnosis: a `MaterialApp` without `PostHogWidget` records events\n  but no replay, with no error. This is the bug here.\n- The \"check each `MaterialApp`\" step: there are two shells, and only one had\n  the wrapper. This is the same mistake the note describes.\n- Step 1 and 2 of the checklist: `posthog_flutter: ^5.36.0` is in\n  `pubspec.yaml` (>= 5.14.0), and `sessionReplay = true` is set in\n  `lib/analytics.dart`.\n- Step 4: `PosthogObserver()` is in both shells (`navigatorObservers` in\n  legacy, `GoRouter.observers` in new), so screen splitting is already in\n  place.\n\nNot applicable, or already satisfied:\n- Step 3, `startSessionRecording()` behind a flag: not used here. Recording is\n  turned on by `config.sessionReplay = true` before setup, which is the\n  documented path.\n- Step 5, `maskAllTexts`: already set to `true` in `analytics.dart`.\n- Web / posthog-js notes: this is a mobile build, not relevant.\n- Sampling, retention, and project-setting checks: the ticket already rules\n  these out.\n\n## Not verified\n\n- I did not run the app on a device or emulator, so the fix is not confirmed\n  end to end. Verify with the steps in the colleague's note: run\n  `flutter run --dart-define=NEW_UI=true` on a device, go through 3-4 screens,\n  background the app, and check that the session appears in the Replay tab\n  with screenshots.\n- `flutter analyze lib/new_app.dart` passes with no issues.\n- Nothing was committed or deployed. The change needs a new release to reach\n  users.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":576,"cache_read_input_tokens":35247,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":576},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"94cd5ac4-6f92-49c7-ada5-aa23ec347386","uuid":"d2bfa34b-6727-4215-b1b0-eff3c75e6427","timestamp":"2026-10-19T02:55:20.407Z","request_id":"req_011CgAqoX6EwQBHnVKhNxvW4","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_016gMT3rMMbre1m5u1HMYsto":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/h-Kf8Lbf/ANSWER.md","content":"# Ticket #4471: why new-UI users have no session replays\n\n## Cause\n\nReplay is built from screenshots taken by `PostHogWidget`. The legacy shell\n(`lib/legacy_app.dart`) wraps its `MaterialApp` in `PostHogWidget`. The new\nshell (`lib/new_app.dart`) builds `MaterialApp.router` without it. So the new\nUI sends events (screens, taps, `loan_amount_changed`, `application_submitted`)\nbut no frames, and the Replay tab only has sessions from the old UI.\n\nEvidence:\n- `posthog_flutter` 5.55.0 source (`lib/src/posthog_widget.dart`): the widget's\n  state creates the `ScreenshotCapturer` and `NativeCommunicator` that feed\n  replay. Nothing else in the package produces replay frames on mobile.\n- Ticket: project settings are fine (recording on, sampling 100%, minimum\n  duration 0) and both groups use the same SDK version and build. The only\n  code difference between the groups is the wrapper.\n- `main.dart` calls `Analytics.init()` (which calls `Posthog().setup`) before\n  `runApp`, so the widget finds a config and starts capturing. Setup order is\n  not the cause.\n\n## Fix\n\n`lib/new_app.dart`: wrapped `MaterialApp.router` in `PostHogWidget` and added a\ncomment saying why it must stay. `dart format` also reflowed the `theme:`\nblock onto one line.\n\nNo other files changed.\n\n## Which parts of the colleague's note applied\n\nApplied:\n- The core diagnosis: a `MaterialApp` without `PostHogWidget` records events\n  but no replay, with no error. This is the bug here.\n- The \"check each `MaterialApp`\" step: there are two shells, and only one had\n  the wrapper. This is the same mistake the note describes.\n- Step 1 and 2 of the checklist: `posthog_flutter: ^5.36.0` is in\n  `pubspec.yaml` (>= 5.14.0), and `sessionReplay = true` is set in\n  `lib/analytics.dart`.\n- Step 4: `PosthogObserver()` is in both shells (`navigatorObservers` in\n  legacy, `GoRouter.observers` in new), so screen splitting is already in\n  place.\n\nNot applicable, or already satisfied:\n- Step 3, `startSessionRecording()` behind a flag: not used here. Recording is\n  turned on by `config.sessionReplay = true` before setup, which is the\n  documented path.\n- Step 5, `maskAllTexts`: already set to `true` in `analytics.dart`.\n- Web / posthog-js notes: this is a mobile build, not relevant.\n- Sampling, retention, and project-setting checks: the ticket already rules\n  these out.\n\n## Not verified\n\n- I did not run the app on a device or emulator, so the fix is not confirmed\n  end to end. Verify with the steps in the colleague's note: run\n  `flutter run --dart-define=NEW_UI=true` on a device, go through 3-4 screens,\n  background the app, and check that the session appears in the Replay tab\n  with screenshots.\n- `flutter analyze lib/new_app.dart` passes with no issues.\n- Nothing was committed or deployed. The change needs a new release to reach\n  users.\n"}}}
